# WHAT IS IN THIS REPOSITORY, stated the only way git can state it: everything
# at the top is ignored, and the handful of things that ARE the program are
# named back in. Written this way round on purpose -- a rule that lists what
# to leave out goes stale the moment something new is dropped in the folder,
# and what turned up here over time was a gigabyte and a half of audio,
# benchmark output, training material and working notes that nobody meant to
# commit.
#
# The program is three directories and the handful of files that start it.
/*

!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore

# the program
!/mild-lyrics/
!/editor/
!/docs/

# ...and what starts it, checks it, and explains it
!/README.md
!/setup.sh
!/setup.cmd
!/mild-setup.py
!/noconsole.py
!/mild-lyrics.pyw
!/ttml-editor.pyw
!/mild-lyrics.desktop
!/ttml-editor.desktop

# ...and what it may be shared under, and whose code it carries
!/LICENSE
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Inside those, the same things that never belong in a repository anywhere.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.opus

# Credentials live in ~/.config/mild-lyrics and ~/.cache/mild-lyrics, never in
# the tree -- but a stray copy in here must not be committable either.
gui.json
editor.json
spicy-key.txt
*token*.json
